# Helm templates are Go-templated YAML, not parseable YAML.
charts/*/templates/

# Claude skills carry a table generated by scripts/gen-claude-skills.py, and
# prettier rewrites the `*` that marks an optional field into `_`, which is a
# different character with a different meaning. Formatting them would corrupt
# the table and then fight the generator on the next run.
.claude/skills/

# Generated by `cargo run -p fastllm-operator --bin crdgen`, and
# `operator/tests/crd_is_current.rs` compares the file byte-for-byte against
# what that produces. Formatting it makes that test fail for ever, which is
# exactly what happened: a tree-wide format run reflowed it and the operator's
# own tests are not in CI, so nobody saw.
operator/deploy/crd.yaml
